==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} ''quincunx''

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|es}}

# An arrangement of five [[unit]]s in a pattern corresponding to the five-spot on [[dice]], playing cards, or [[domino]]es.
# {{context|astrology|lang=en}} An [[angle]] of five-twelfths of a circle, or 150°, between two objects.
# A [[bronze]] [[coin]] minted during the [[Rome|Roman Republic]], valued at five-twelfths of an [[as]].

